  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Nevada drilled for power and accidentally built a geyser. Fly Ranch, in the desert west of the Black Rock. It has not stopped since 1964.",
        "visual_query": "nevada desert geyser hot spring",
        "visual_fallback": "desert geyser"
      },
      {
        "narration": "A geothermal company sank a well there, found the water too cool to be worth anything, and capped it off. The seal failed.",
        "visual_query": "desert drilling rig nevada flats",
        "visual_fallback": "drilling rig"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Hot water has been pushing out of it ever since, loaded with dissolved calcium carbonate and silica. And every litre leaves a little of that behind.",
        "visual_query": "steaming mineral hot spring terraces",
        "visual_fallback": "steaming spring"
      },
      {
        "narration": "So it is still growing. Mineral cones, stepped pools, a mound now roughly thirty feet, built by a mistake nobody fixed.",
        "visual_query": "travertine terrace pools rising steam",
        "visual_fallback": "travertine pools"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The scarlet and green are heat-loving microbes living in the runoff. In 2016 Burning Man's nonprofit bought the entire ranch, geyser included, for six and a half million dollars.",
        "visual_query": "black rock desert playa nevada",
        "visual_fallback": "desert playa"
      }
    ],
